@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 PostgreSQL writes: JPA entities, JDBC batches, partitions and PL/pgSQL

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #253746
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #334155
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #334155
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam participantFontColor #111827
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5CC
skinparam noteBorderColor #8A5A00
skinparam noteFontColor #111827
skinparam groupBorderColor #334155
skinparam groupHeaderBackgroundColor #E5E7EB
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam maxMessageSize 220

participant "REST / Actor / Scheduler" as Entry
participant "Domain Service" as Service
participant "Spring TX Proxy" as Tx
participant "JpaAbstractDao" as JpaDao
participant "JpaRepository / Hibernate" as Hibernate
participant "Async SQL DAO" as AsyncDao
participant "SQL Blocking Queue" as SqlQueue
participant "JdbcTemplate Repository" as Jdbc
participant "Partition Repository" as Partition
participant "Alarm Repository" as AlarmRepo
participant "HikariCP" as Pool
database "PostgreSQL" as PG
participant "WAL / Storage" as WAL
participant "After-Commit Listener" as AfterCommit
participant "Kafka Consumer" as Kafka

== Path A: Device entity and credentials ==
Entry -> Service : DeviceController.saveDevice(device)
Service -> Tx : enter public @Transactional method
Tx -> Pool : borrow JDBC connection
Pool --> Tx : connection bound to thread
Service -> Service : validate tenant, profile and device data
Service -> JpaDao : saveAndFlush(tenant, device)
JpaDao -> JpaDao : construct DeviceEntity
alt new entity
  JpaDao -> JpaDao : Uuids.timeBased()\ncreated_time from UUID
end
JpaDao -> Hibernate : JpaRepository.save(entity)
Hibernate -> PG : INSERT or UPDATE device
JpaDao -> Hibernate : flush()
Hibernate -> PG : execute SQL and constraints now
Service -> JpaDao : create device credentials
JpaDao -> Hibernate : save credentials entity
Hibernate -> PG : INSERT device_credentials
Service -> AfterCommit : publish cache evict event inside TX
Service --> Tx : return
Tx -> PG : COMMIT
PG -> WAL : WAL flush per PostgreSQL settings
WAL --> PG : commit durability acknowledgement
PG --> Tx : commit success
Tx -> Pool : return connection
Tx -> AfterCommit : TransactionalEventListener
AfterCommit -> AfterCommit : evict device and credentials cache
Tx --> Entry : saved Device
note over JpaDao,Tx
  flush is not commit. A later credentials failure still rolls back the outer transaction.
end note

== Path B: Attribute JDBC batch ==
Entry -> Service : save attributes list
loop each AttributeKvEntry
  Service -> AsyncDao : save(tenant, entity, scope, entry)
  AsyncDao -> SqlQueue : add(AttributeKvEntity)
end
note over SqlQueue
  Entity UUID hash selects one local writer.
  The LinkedBlockingQueue has no configured capacity.
end note
SqlQueue -> SqlQueue : poll first and drain to batch size
SqlQueue -> SqlQueue : optionally sort full composite key
SqlQueue -> Jdbc : saveOrUpdate(batch)
Jdbc -> Tx : TransactionTemplate opens batch transaction
Tx -> Pool : borrow connection
Jdbc -> PG : batch UPDATE existing attributes
PG --> Jdbc : JDBC update counts
Jdbc -> Jdbc : collect rows with update count zero
Jdbc -> PG : batch INSERT ON CONFLICT
alt batch transaction commits
  Jdbc --> SqlQueue : return
  SqlQueue --> AsyncDao : all batch Futures success
  AsyncDao --> Service : allAsList success
else any SQL error
  PG --> Tx : exception
  Tx -> PG : ROLLBACK whole batch
  Jdbc --> SqlQueue : throw
  SqlQueue --> AsyncDao : all batch Futures failed
end
note over Jdbc,PG
  attribute last_update_ts is stored but is not used as an update predicate.
  An older write submitted later can overwrite a newer value.
end note

== Path C: SQL telemetry partition and batch ==
Entry -> AsyncDao : save TsKvEntry with database.ts.type=sql
AsyncDao -> AsyncDao : compute UTC period start/end
alt partition cache miss
  AsyncDao -> Partition : save(SqlPartition)
  Partition -> Tx : NOT_SUPPORTED suspends parent transaction
  Partition -> Pool : borrow independent connection
  Partition -> PG : CREATE TABLE ... PARTITION OF ts_kv
  alt created
    PG --> Partition : success
  else already exists, overlap or default contains rows
    PG --> Partition : DDL error
    Partition --> AsyncDao : catch known race / warn
  end
end
AsyncDao -> SqlQueue : add(TsKvEntity)
SqlQueue -> Jdbc : saveOrUpdate(history batch)
Jdbc -> Tx : begin repository transaction
Jdbc -> PG : INSERT parent ts_kv ON CONFLICT
PG -> PG : route row to range child\nor ts_kv_indefinite DEFAULT
alt commit
  PG --> Jdbc : success
  Jdbc --> SqlQueue : return
  SqlQueue --> AsyncDao : history Future success
else failure
  PG --> Jdbc : exception and rollback
  SqlQueue --> AsyncDao : Future failure
end

== Path D: Alarm PL/pgSQL state transition ==
Entry -> Service : create / ack / clear Alarm
Service -> AlarmRepo : native repository method
AlarmRepo -> Tx : join or open transaction
Tx -> Pool : borrow connection
AlarmRepo -> PG : SELECT create_or_update_active_alarm(...)
PG -> PG : find active alarm
alt existing row
  PG -> PG : SELECT ... FOR UPDATE
  PG -> PG : validate state and UPDATE tuple
else no existing row
  PG -> PG : INSERT new alarm
end
PG --> AlarmRepo : JSON result
AlarmRepo --> Service : AlarmApiCallResult
Service --> Tx : return
Tx -> PG : COMMIT
note over AlarmRepo,PG
  FOR UPDATE serializes an existing row.
  First concurrent creation has no row to lock and the active index is not unique.
end note

== Kafka and database are separate commits ==
Kafka -> Entry : submit polled Rule Engine message
Entry -> Service : execute rule nodes
Service -> PG : one or more independent DB transactions
PG --> Service : committed
Service --> Kafka : callback success
Kafka -> Kafka : commitSync offset according processing strategy
note over Kafka,PG
  There is no XA or outbox transaction.
  A crash after DB commit and before offset commit causes replay.
end note

== Connection pressure ==
Entry -> Pool : synchronous JPA request
AsyncDao -> Pool : JpaExecutor task
SqlQueue -> Pool : attribute/history/latest/event workers
alt idle connection available
  Pool --> Entry : connection
else all 16 default connections busy
  Pool -> Pool : borrower waits until timeout or return
end
note over Pool,PG
  maximumPoolSize is per service instance.
  Cluster capacity is the sum of all service pools and other clients.
end note

== SQL telemetry TTL ==
Entry -> Partition : scheduled cleanup on owner
Partition -> PG : CALL drop_partitions_by_system_ttl
PG -> PG : DROP fully expired range children
Partition -> PG : CALL cleanup_timeseries_by_ttl
PG -> PG : DELETE rows for tenant/customer TTL
note over Partition,PG
  Row UPDATE/DELETE creates dead tuples.
  VACUUM progress, long snapshots and WAL/checkpoint pressure affect write latency.
end note
@enduml
